   "bands": "Top/bottom band = the 2 highest / lowest weekly scores (three, or half the league when it has fewer than six teams; this league has 4). Descriptive ranks, not thresholds that predict anything.",
   "counterfactual": "Counterfactual: keep the selected team's actual score each period and compare it with the actual score of the opponent the other manager faced that period. A period where that opponent is the selected team itself is excluded. These are hypothetical opponent assignments, not a valid reconstructed league schedule; the hypothetical result compares points (ESPN tiebreaks are not applied). Actual and counterfactual records use exactly the same periods.",
   "eligible": "A period is eligible only when every league team has exactly one completed regular-season two-team matchup with both scores present. Otherwise it is excluded for every team (reasons listed), so no team is compared with an incomplete pool.",
   "expected": "Expected wins in a period = (teams outscored + 0.5 x teams tied) / (teams - 1), comparing a team's matchup-period score with every other team's score in the same period. Season expected wins = the sum over eligible periods. An all-play win equivalent, not a probability of winning the actual matchup.",
   "luck": "Schedule luck = actual win equivalents (win 1, tie 0.5) minus expected wins, over the same eligible periods. Positive: more actual wins than the weekly scoring rank implies. An observed result gap, not proof of luck or skill and not a prediction of regression.",
   "result_source": "Actual results are ESPN's winner field; a points tie that ESPN broke with a league tiebreak counts as ESPN recorded it."
  },
